## Bench isolation made for the run (STANDING-ORDERS §6: once before the TestSet, once after)
Same two-leg LAG isolation as T33234 (the frame binds `cusfp` before `copper` and sorts non-LAG
links first, so BOTH sa2 legs must be free for the copper role to land on a non-LAG port):
- stack (u2): vlan 3999 + port1.0.9 out of sa2 into VLAN 3999 (12:13:54); vlan 3998 + port1.0.2
  `shutdown` / `no static-channel-group` / `switchport access vlan 3998` / `no shutdown` (12:1x)
- x230 (u0): vlan 3999 + port1.0.4 into VLAN 3999 (12:14:18); vlan 3998 + port1.0.3 out of sa2
  into VLAN 3998
- `interface sa2` auto-deleted on both ends once its last member left (`% Can't find interface sa2.`)
Run binding (run.stdout 12:17:48):
  topology: role 'cusfp'  -> swi_a port1.0.2 <-> swi_f port1.0.3 (cusfp)
  BENCH PROBLEM, not a product defect: no unused fibre link on swi_a (data links discovered: 1 tb,
    5 cusfp). Cable a fibre partner port to the DUT and declare it under [portlink]. This role is
    OPTIONAL here: the cases needing it report UNSUPPORTED.
  topology: role 'copper' -> swi_a port1.0.9 <-> swi_f port1.0.4 (cusfp)
Test link = stack member 1 port1.0.9 (AT-SPTXc, RJ45) <-> x230-10GP port1.0.4 (fixed copper).
Monitored copper-SFP port = port1.0.2 <-> x230 port1.0.3.

